window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-f111c1fd1f0ed41b"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"analyze-kpi-root-causes\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"kpi\">分析 KPI 变化的根本原因</h1> <p>用证据解释指标的意外变动，并提出后续行动。</p> <p>向 ChatGPT 提供 KPI 仪表盘、指标定义、数据导出、细分维度、发布背景和利益相关方讨论，然后请它在有来源支持的根因简报中区分已确认的驱动因素与待验证假设。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>正在调查 KPI 意外变动的产品、增长或运营团队。</li> <li>需要按细分群体、群组、渠道、地域或产品维度拆解的根因问题。</li> <li>必须把已确认驱动因素与合理假设分开呈现的审查工作。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>检查指标数据导出、计算不同维度的切分结果，并制作辅助图表。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive（需联网）</a></td> <td>阅读指标定义、仪表盘、发布背景和获准使用的来源文件。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack（需联网）</a></td> <td>查看相关利益相关方背景和近期变化。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>将分析整理成便于审阅、附有来源和注意事项的简报。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">起步提示词</h2> <p>找出 KPI 变化的根本原因</p> <p>建议模型：<code>gpt-6-luna</code> · 建议推理级别：<code>xhigh</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请解释 [KPI] 在 [time window] 内发生变化的原因。\n\n请使用我提供的 KPI 仪表盘、指标定义、来源数据导出、细分维度、发布或营销活动背景，以及利益相关方讨论。按相关的细分群体、群组、渠道、地域和产品界面拆解变化。\n\n请返回一份根因简报，包括：\n- 图表和重要变化\n- 已确认的驱动因素\n- 有待调查的假设\n- 注意事项和数据质量问题\n- 来源链接\n- 未解决的问题\n- 建议采取的行动\n\n不要把相关性当作因果关系的证明，也不要修改来源数据。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/codex-for-work/how-data-science-teams-use-codex/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy：数据科学团队（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-99d1e8fe39794227\">查询表格数据</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可查看该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"define-the-metric-before-explaining-movement\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">解释变化前，先定义指标</h2> <p>根因分析要从稳定的指标定义、对比时间范围和可信来源数据开始。请先向 ChatGPT 提供 KPI 定义、仪表盘、数据导出，以及发布或营销活动背景，再让它解释变化。</p> <ol> <li>说明 KPI、对比时段、预期变化方向，以及分析需要支持的决策。</li> <li>附上仪表盘、指标定义、数据导出、细分结果和相关背景。</li> <li>请 ChatGPT 检查数据质量，并提出最有用的拆解维度。</li> <li>运行起始提示词；审阅时把已确认的驱动因素与假设分开。</li> <li>修改仪表盘或流程前，先让指标负责人核实建议行动。</li> </ol> <p>用图表让变化过程可以检查，但不要把某个细分维度与指标的相关性当作原因证明。请在简报中保留来源链接、注意事项和未解决问题。</p> <p><a id=\"challenge-the-root-cause\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">质疑根因结论</h2> <p>在把简报交给管理层前，请 ChatGPT 寻找反面证据和其它可能的解释。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Challenge the root-cause brief.\n\nFor each confirmed driver or hypothesis, list:\n\n- supporting source and calculation\n- counterevidence or alternative explanation\n- segment or cohort where it does not hold\n- data-quality limitation\n- next check that would increase confidence\n\nRevise the recommendation only when the evidence supports it, and keep all changes visible.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">质疑这份根因简报。\n\n针对每个已确认的影响因素或假设，列出：\n\n- 支持它的来源和计算\n- 反证或其他解释\n- 它不成立的细分群体或同期群\n- 数据质量方面的局限\n- 能提高判断信心的下一项检查\n\n只有证据支持时才修订建议，并让所有变更保持可见。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"analyze-kpi-root-causes\">Analyze KPI root causes</h1> <p>Explain an unexpected metric movement with evidence and next actions.</p> <p>Give ChatGPT KPI dashboards, metric definitions, exports, segment cuts, launch context, and stakeholder threads, then ask it to separate confirmed drivers from hypotheses in a source-backed root-cause brief.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Product, growth, or operations teams investigating an unexpected KPI movement.</li> <li>Root-cause questions that require segment, cohort, channel, geography, or product cuts.</li> <li>Reviews where confirmed drivers must stay separate from plausible hypotheses.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>Inspect metric exports, calculate cuts, and create supporting charts.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive (online)</a></td> <td>Read metric definitions, dashboards, launch context, and approved source files.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack (online)</a></td> <td>Check relevant stakeholder context and recent changes.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>Package the analysis as a reviewable brief with sources and caveats.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Find the KPI root cause</p> <p>Suggested model：<code>gpt-6-luna</code> · Suggested reasoning effort：<code>xhigh</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Explain why [KPI] changed during [time window].\n\nUse the KPI dashboard, metric definition, source exports, segment cuts, launch or campaign context, and stakeholder threads I provide. Break down the movement by relevant segment, cohort, channel, geography, and product surface.\n\nReturn a root-cause brief with:\n- charts and material changes\n- confirmed drivers\n- hypotheses to investigate\n- caveats and data-quality issues\n- source links\n- open questions\n- recommended actions\n\nDo not treat correlation as proof, and do not change the source data.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/codex-for-work/how-data-science-teams-use-codex/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy: Data science teams (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-99d1e8fe39794227\">Query tabular data</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"define-the-metric-before-explaining-movement\">Define the metric before explaining movement</h2> <p>Root-cause work starts with a stable definition, comparison window, and source-of-truth data. Give ChatGPT the KPI definition, dashboard, exports, and context around launches or campaigns before asking it to explain the change.</p> <ol> <li>State the KPI, comparison period, expected direction, and decision the analysis should support.</li> <li>Attach the dashboard, metric definition, exports, segment cuts, and relevant context.</li> <li>Ask ChatGPT to inspect data quality and propose the most useful breakdowns.</li> <li>Run the starter prompt and review confirmed drivers separately from hypotheses.</li> <li>Validate the recommended actions with the metric owner before changing a dashboard or process.</li> </ol> <p>Use charts to make the movement inspectable, but do not treat a segment correlation as proof of cause. Keep source links, caveats, and open questions with the brief.</p> <h2 id=\"challenge-the-root-cause\">Challenge the root cause</h2> <p>Ask ChatGPT to look for counterevidence and alternative explanations before the brief goes to leadership.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Challenge the root-cause brief.\n\nFor each confirmed driver or hypothesis, list:\n\n- supporting source and calculation\n- counterevidence or alternative explanation\n- segment or cohort where it does not hold\n- data-quality limitation\n- next check that would increase confidence\n\nRevise the recommendation only when the evidence supports it, and keep all changes visible.\n</code></pre>"};
